### Only stop positively identified runners from this checkout

**Severity:** `medium`

The current filter drops instances whose executable `Path` is unavailable, so they fall through to the subsequent `Stop-Process` call. Its wildcard also treats an adjacent directory such as `C:\Dev\PowerToysClone` as belonging to `C:\Dev\PowerToys`. Refuse unknown or unreadable paths, require a literal directory boundary, and avoid reading an unavailable path again in the warning.

```suggestion
    $installed = $running | Where-Object {
        try {
            $path = $_.Path
            -not $path -or -not $path.StartsWith("$($repoRoot.TrimEnd('\'))\", [StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)
        } catch {
            $true
        }
    }
    if ($installed) {
        Write-Warning "Another PowerToys instance is running outside this checkout, or its executable path could not be verified. Exit it first; two runners compete for keyboard hooks and hotkeys."
```

### Probe essentials in the selected platform's output

**Severity:** `medium`

These probes use `x64` even when the requested platform is ARM64, so existing x64 Settings and Quick Access outputs can incorrectly satisfy the readiness checks. The runner probe also looks under `WinUI3Apps`, although the runner output copied below comes from its project output directory. Probe the actual runner output and the selected platform's managed apps; apply this together with the runtime-layout correction.

```suggestion
    @{ Exe = "src\runner\$Platform\$Configuration\PowerToys.exe"; Project = "src\runner\Runner.vcxproj"; Name = "Runner" }
    @{ Exe = "$Platform\$Configuration\WinUI3Apps\PowerToys.Settings.exe"; Project = "src\settings-ui\Settings.UI\PowerToys.Settings.csproj"; Name = "Settings UI" }
    @{ Exe = "$Platform\$Configuration\WinUI3Apps\PowerToys.QuickAccess.exe"; Project = "src\settings-ui\QuickAccess.UI\PowerToys.QuickAccess.csproj"; Name = "Quick Access" }
```
